 "about": {
  "what": "Morphology package: the body of one creature as a topological entity (nodes, edges, parameters).",
  "frame": "x forward, y to the creature's left, z up; lengths in the generator's units (see 'size')",
  "nodes": "one per joint of each placed copy of a part; id = <part>[.<copy>].j<index>; index 0 is where the part starts",
  "bones": "one per stretch between neighbouring nodes; id = <part>[.<copy>].b<index>; 'parent' is the bone it moves with",
  "edges": "bone: two nodes of one chain. attach: first node of a part to a bone of its parent part, at 't' along that bone (0 = start, 1 = end). mirror: the same node on the left and right copy. radial: the same node on neighbouring copies around the parent.",
  "parts": "one per gene of the genome; 'copies' lists the placed copies ('' = single, L/R = mirrored, 0..N-1 = radial)",
  "groups": "named sets of part names, for addressing several parts at once",
  "skin": "per mesh vertex: up to 4 bones (indices into 'bones') and their weights (sum 1). A default binding; a motion system may ignore it and bind the mesh its own way.",
  "access": "read_only: a motion system may move nodes (pose) but not add, remove or rewire them. The body is grown from the genome; a change to its structure has to go back to RTIS as a gene change, and RTIS grows a new body and a new package.",
  "lineage": "how this body came to be. Inheritance is done by RTIS on genes; a motion system receives the result here and does not redo it. ancestry_a per part = share of the part's genes from parent A."
 },
